  "summary": "I wrote src/main.ts and it passes `typecheck`. I could not run it, so I haven't seen a rendered frame, and `vite build` and the headless Chromium run are untested. The scene has a ground plane plus three instanced nodes, which is three draw calls for 10,000 objects:\n- **Trees:** 8,000 instanced trunks (cylinders) and 8,000 instanced canopies (cones).\n- **Rocks:** 2,000 instanced spheres.\n- **Placement:** a seeded LCG random generator places everything inside a 62-unit disc, so the forest is the same on every load.\n- **Colour variation:** each canopy gets a random HSL green and each rock a random grey-brown. Both use a white base material so the instance colours show unchanged.\n- **Light and fog:** one directional light with shadows (a single 4096 shadow map fitted to the forest) and a hemisphere fill light. The exponential fog uses density 0.004 and matches the background colour.\n- **Camera:** an orbit camera set high and back so the whole forest is in view. It turns slowly through `interactions.orbit({ autoRotate: 0.12 })`, which the docs describe but which I haven't seen move.\n- **Ready flag:** `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set after `app.ready()` and once `onFrame` has fired at least once.\n\n",
